  "notes": "WRITING:\n- {妥|だ} - peaceful settlement\n- {協|きょう} - cooperation\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {妥協|だきょう}する - to compromise\n- {妥協|だきょう}を{許|ゆる}さない - to allow no compromise\n- {妥協点|だきょうてん} - point of compromise\n- {妥協案|だきょうあん} - compromise proposal\n- {妥協|だきょう}に{達|たっ}する - to reach a compromise\n- {妥協|だきょう}の{余地|よち} - room for compromise\n\nNEGATIVE USE:\n{妥協|だきょう}しない is often used as a positive trait, meaning refusing to lower one's standards:\n- {品質|ひんしつ}に{妥協|だきょう}しない - uncompromising on quality\n- {味|あじ}に{妥協|だきょう}しない - no compromise on taste\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {譲歩|じょうほ} - concession, giving in\n- {折|お}り{合|あ}い - settlement, understanding\n- {歩|あゆ}み{寄|よ}り - meeting halfway\n\nREGISTER:\nNeutral. Common in business, politics, and everyday discussion.",
